  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0 (cut from upstream/main 7580cd21).\n\nDocs only (`site/content/`). Adds the macOS equivalent beside each Windows-specific instruction on the pages the issue lists.\n\n## What changed per page\n\n- **guide/first-run.md**: a note under \"The window\" that the shortcuts are written with Ctrl and that macOS uses Cmd (the app binds them through egui's command modifier, `crates/ui/src/egui_app/panes.rs`). Right-click to pin an operation now also lists Control-click and a two-finger click on a Mac. The Undo section gives Cmd+Z / Cmd+Y beside Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y.\n- **guide/install.md**: the macOS section names the app executable `CamCraft.app/Contents/MacOS/camcraft-ui`, the CLI (`camcraft-cli`) and `post` in the same folder, and the release files `camcraft-<version>-macos-universal.dmg` and `.zip`. All from `scripts/package-macos.sh`. The Windows section is unchanged.\n- **guide/operations.md**: undo gives Cmd+Z; Alt+click gives Option+click on macOS.\n- **guide/posting.md**: Post gives Cmd+P beside Ctrl+P.\n- **developers/commands.md**: undo and redo give Cmd+Z / Cmd+Y beside Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y.\n- **developers/gates.md**: `scripts/gate.ps1` is labelled PowerShell and `scripts/gate.sh` bash; states that `cargo xtask gate` is the same command on Windows, macOS and Linux.\n\nShortcut check against source (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/panes.rs`): Ctrl+N, O, Shift+O, S, Shift+S, P, Z, Y are bound through `modifiers.command`; the Q quit binding is also there but is not documented on these pages. Ctrl+click and Shift+click for edges are in `crates/ui/src/edge_pick.rs` and `geo_page.rs`; Alt+click for a single segment is in `boundary.rs` and `geo_page.rs`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The site was not built: `zola` is not installed on this machine, so `zola check` and `zola build` were not run.\n- No page was viewed in a browser.\n\n## Unconfirmed (not written into the site, needs a Mac)\n\n- **Gatekeeper on macOS 15 (Sequoia) and later.** The existing \"Control-click, then Open\" text is kept. The System Settings > Privacy & Security > Open Anyway route, and the `xattr` command, were not added: neither is in the repo, and both need a current Mac to confirm.\n- **Control-click and two-finger click as a right-click** for pinning. The issue suggests them; it is macOS behaviour, not checked in the repo, and not run on a Mac.\n- **Ctrl+click picking an edge on a Mac.** `edge_pick.rs` reads `mods.ctrl`, but on macOS Control-click is the system secondary click and may not reach the pick. Not documented on any page; needs a Mac check and a ui bug if it fails.\n- **Alt = Option on macOS.** This mapping is egui's convention, not something the repo states. Used on the operations page.\n- **Build from source on macOS.** The cargo commands are unchanged; the Xcode Command Line Tools requirement (`xcode-select --install`) is not stated anywhere in the repo, so it was not added.\n- **Hint strings in the UI.** `op_page.rs` and `machines_pane.rs` still say \"Ctrl+Z undoes\" on hover, and `geo_page.rs` says \"Ctrl+click\". These are product strings, out of scope for a docs-only change. Candidate for a follow-up ui issue.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #1236\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
